def sportpress_ui_strings(
    *,
    return_parsed: bool = True,
    return_as_pandas: bool = False,
    **kwargs,
) -> Union[pl.DataFrame, pd.DataFrame, Dict]:
    """UI string tables of the site in English, French and Dutch (one row per language and key).

    Endpoint: ``GET https://bnxt.sportpress.info/api/v1/server-config``
    Example URL: https://bnxt.sportpress.info/api/v1/server-config

    Args:
        return_parsed: parse the payload through parse_sportpress_ui_strings -> polars DataFrame (default True). Pass return_parsed=False for the raw body (``dict``): ``{'data': ...}`` (the settings object for the site config, the nine-category object for the rankings) with contact fields dropped, plus ``_request`` (the season, competition, team, roster or game ids asked for).
        return_as_pandas: with return_parsed, return a pandas DataFrame instead of polars.
        **kwargs: Forwarded to the underlying HTTP getter.

    Returns:
        A polars/pandas DataFrame by default; the raw body (``dict``): ``{'data': ...}`` (the settings object for the site config, the nine-category object for the rankings) with contact fields dropped, plus ``_request`` (the season, competition, team, roster or game ids asked for) when ``return_parsed=False``.

    Raises:
        sportsdataverse.errors.NoDataError: the API has nothing for the request (HTTP 404, an empty ``data`` list: an unknown id or a season without data, an empty ranking).
        sportsdataverse.errors.AssetFetchError: the fetch failed or the answer is not the one asked for (a rejected key: 'key rotated?', an error or changed envelope, a game that is not finished, a body for another season, competition, team or game).

    Example:
        Quick start::

            from sportsdataverse.basketball.bnxt import sportpress_ui_strings
            sportpress_ui_strings()

        See Also:
            * `BNXT League`_ - the site whose Sportpress backend these wrappers read
            * `wehoop`_ - SportsDataverse women's basketball (R)
            * `hoopR`_ - SportsDataverse men's basketball (R)

        .. _BNXT League: https://bnxtleague.com
        .. _wehoop: https://wehoop.sportsdataverse.org
        .. _hoopR: https://hoopR.sportsdataverse.org

    Notes:
        * Unofficial and unsupported: the Sportpress API is the JSON backend of bnxtleague.com, not a documented public API. Every route needs a header key; it is public (hard-coded in the site bundle), ``bnxt_runtime`` reads it from the bundle at run time, falls back to a documented value when the bundle cannot be read, and never prints or logs it. A 401 raises AssetFetchError (``key rotated?``). robots.txt allows everything; requests are spaced at least 1 s apart. Payloads are not redistributed as release assets.
        * Season key: the END year (``season=2026`` is 2025-26), the API's own key on the season routes. Every other route is keyed by the competition id (one per season: 1 = 2021-22, 2 = 2020-21, 3 = 2022-23, 12 = 2023-24, 22 = 2024-25, 24 = 2025-26, 25 = 2026-27), the competition-team id (new every season; ``uu_team_id`` is the stable club), the roster id (player x team x season) or the game id (unique across seasons). ``sportpress_phases(season)`` maps a season to its competition id.
        * Coverage: schedule and rosters from 2021-22 (2020-21 is empty); box scores for 2021-22, 2024-25, 2025-26 and 2026-27 (2022-23 and 2023-24 answer empty); standings and averages for 2021-22 and 2024-25 on; play-by-play ('film', with court x/y) for 2021-22 and 2026-27 only: for 2022-23 to 2025-26 use Genius play-by-play through ``genius_id`` (``sportpress_game_slider``, organisation BNXT). The game routes (box score, film, overview) refuse a game that is not finished (AssetFetchError).
        * Data notes: a team's box total can differ from the schedule final score on about 18 of 1,246 sampled team boxes (mostly 2024-25, by 2-21 points); the frames report what the API serves. ``nationality_code`` is dirty (lower case, ``USA/BEL`` pairs, empty, ``HOL``). Names differ by language and sponsor: join on ids. Contact and social fields are dropped; only a player's public birth date is kept. The sibling tenants sopron.sportpress.info and beac.sportpress.info are not wrapped.
    """
    _caller_params = kwargs.pop("params", None) or {}
    _params = {}
    _params.update(_caller_params)
    raw = _get(
        "https://bnxt.sportpress.info/api/v1/server-config",
        params=_params,
        **kwargs,
    )
    if return_parsed:
        return parse_sportpress_ui_strings(
            raw, return_as_pandas=return_as_pandas, columns=_PARSER_COLUMNS["ui_strings"]
        )
    return raw


